# Draft knowledge entry: open62541 OHOS musl stdio limit header

id: DRAFT-open62541-ohos-musl-stdio-lim-1.5.6
trigger_tool: cc|clang|cmake|conan
phase: compilation
error_signature: fatal error: 'bits/stdio_lim.h' file not found
severity: 2
category: compat|libc|musl|header|open62541
match_keywords: open62541, eventloop_posix.h, bits/stdio_lim.h, OHOS, musl, glibc-only header, aarch64
title: open62541 POSIX event loop must guard glibc-only bits/stdio_lim.h by libc capability
root_cause: >
  OHOS uses a musl-based libc surface and does not provide glibc's private
  bits/stdio_lim.h header. The upstream generic Linux platform condition
  includes it even though the OHOS SDK is not a glibc sysroot.
affected_scope: >
  open62541 POSIX event-loop builds targeting the HarmonyOS OHOS SDK, and
  similar C projects that use Linux-like preprocessor macros to select glibc
  private headers.
verification_cmd: >
  conan create archives/o/open62541/1.5.6 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64
  -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 --build=missing;
  verify that the consumer compiles and links as ELF64 AArch64.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: glibc-capability-guard-private-header
rec_description: >
  Guard the bits/stdio_lim.h include with defined(__GLIBC__) and retain the
  upstream include only for glibc environments that provide it. Do not add a
  fake glibc header to the OHOS sysroot or introduce a platform macro.
rec_command: >
  Apply patches/0001-arch-posix-eventloop_posix.h.patch, then run the OHOS
  Conan create and consumer test.
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: open62541-ohos-portability-patch
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: inspect-libc-sysroot
fallback_description: >
  Confirm the active OHOS sysroot and libc before changing source guards; a
  missing header must not be fixed by copying host glibc headers.
fallback_command: grep -R "stdio_lim.h" "$OHOS_SYSROOT/usr/include" 2>/dev/null
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: sysroot-header-audit
forbid_1_pattern: copy host glibc bits/stdio_lim.h into OHOS sysroot
forbid_1_reason: Host glibc private headers are not ABI-compatible with the OHOS libc surface.
forbid_1_consequence: The package becomes non-reproducible and can fail later at link or runtime.
principles: musl-glibc-boundary, scoped-platform-guard, consumer-verification
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: []
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
